// "You get {E}" ([CR#107.14] — {E} is the energy symbol, one energy counter;
// getting it puts that many energy counters on you, which sit on the player
// [CR#122.1]): a `OneShotEffect` that puts that many energy counters on you.
// The sibling of `PayEnergy` (the cost side), riding the SAME count-driven
// literal-repetition construct
// `${0*\{E\}}`: the escaped `{E}` literal repeats `${0}`-many times, folded
// back from a run of `{E}` on the parse side.
//
// The param is a PLAIN `Uint` (energy is always a fixed literal count — the
// dynamic "you get {E} for each …" / "an amount of {E} equal to …" forms are a
// different, out-of-scope shape); the body wraps it as `Literal(Param(0))`
// because `PutCounters`'s amount is a `Count`. (`PutCounters` is the positional
// `(Reference, CounterRef, Count)` verb; `Energy` is the counter name minted by
// the `Energy` counter macro.)
(
    name: "GainEnergy",
    template: "you get ${0*\\{E\\}}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    params: [Uint],
    body: PutCounters(You, Energy, Literal(Param(0))),
)
